{%- comment -%}
  Pakket-matcher: scenario cards + comparison table, scored client-side. Single source of
  truth, rendered from three places:
    - sections/vergelijk-pakketten.liquid (the standalone /pages/vergelijk-pakketten page,
      Langer Thuis only)
    - sections/oplossingen.liquid, embedded under the Langer Thuis pricing cards
    - sections/oplossingen.liquid, embedded under the Mijn Thuis pricing cards
  Scoring/highlight JS lives in assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.js (static asset, not a
  section {% javascript %} block, because {% javascript %}/{% stylesheet %} only work in
  section files — not in snippets — see snippets/zv-actie-card.liquid for the same note).
  Both callers must load assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.css and .js themselves (once each,
  outside this snippet) and must have already run {%- include 'zv-pricing' -%}.

  Originally Langer Thuis-only (3 hardcoded packages: inzicht/zeker/beschermd). Generalized
  2026-09-15 to also serve Mijn Thuis (secure/guard/secure_plus) — every new param below is
  OPTIONAL and defaults to reproducing the original Langer Thuis output byte-for-byte, so
  the two existing call sites needed no changes.

  Params (existing, unchanged):
    scenarios              required. `section.blocks | where: 'type', 'scenario'`.
    activation_variant_id  required. All_products[zv_activation_handle]'s variant id.
    collection              optional. Handle/object of the packages collection. Falls back
                            to the 'langer-thuis' collection if blank/empty.
    pm_heading, pm_sub, advies_label, cta_label, cta_added, cta_view_cart, match_badge
                            optional editorial copy, shared across every package.
    opl_url                 optional, defaults to '/pages/oplossingen'.
    embedded                optional, defaults to false. When true, the comparison table's
                            "Kies …" row adds the matching package to cart directly instead
                            of linking to opl_url — see assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.js's
                            addPackageToCart(). Ignored for a package listed in
                            `lead_only_pkgs` (see below), which is always a plain link.
    package_names           zv_package_names_by_fk from zv-pricing. Package display names
                            (products JSON, default pkg_meta) come from it via finder_key,
                            never the product title. Optional only for backward
                            compatibility; every caller passes it.
    zv_inzicht_monthly / zv_zeker_monthly / zv_beschermd_monthly, tagline_inzicht /
    tagline_zeker / tagline_beschermd
                            optional. Only used to build the DEFAULT `pkg_meta` (below) when
                            the caller doesn't pass one — i.e. only Langer Thuis's two call
                            sites still rely on these; a new line should just pass `pkg_meta`
                            directly instead of adding more named price/tagline params here.

  Params (new, all optional — generalization surface):
    pkg_meta                '§'-joined records, one per package, each
                            `id|display name|price|unit|tagline`, e.g.
                            `secure|Alert|{{ zv_alert_monthly }}|/mnd|Basisbeveiliging tegen inbraak`
                            (never a literal amount — see scripts/check_pricing.py check #9).
                            Leave
                            `unit` empty for a non-recurring price (Vista's "Op maat" has no
                            "/mnd"). Order = tier, ascending (see `recommend()` in the JS: a
                            scenario's `package` is the lowest tier that has it, and the
                            advice is the highest of those tiers among the selected cards,
                            i.e. the smallest package that covers all of them — same
                            convention as today's inzicht<zeker<beschermd).
                            Also drives the feature-table's column order and the JS's
                            per-instance TIER/NAMES maps (emitted as data attributes, so two
                            matcher instances with different package vocabularies can coexist
                            on the same page — see assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.js).
                            Default: built from zv_inzicht_monthly/zv_zeker_monthly/
                            zv_beschermd_monthly + tagline_inzicht/zeker/beschermd, i.e.
                            today's exact Langer Thuis 3 packages.
    recommended_pkg         which pkg_meta id gets the "Meest gekozen" badge + gold CTA.
                            Default 'zeker'.
    finder_key_map          'fk:pid,fk:pid,…' — custom.finder_key metafield value -> the
                            internal package id used above. Default
                            'aware:inzicht,aware_plus:zeker,care:beschermd' (today's mapping).
                            Mijn Thuis passes an identity mapping
                            ('secure:secure,guard:guard,secure_plus:secure_plus') since its
                            internal ids are just its finder_key values verbatim.
    feature_rows            '§'-joined comparison-table rows, each
                            `feat|small|val1|val2|val3` (val = 'y', 'n', or literal text) in
                            the same order as pkg_meta. Default: today's exact 8-row Langer
                            Thuis string.
    lead_only_pkgs          comma list of pkg_meta ids that have no cart action at all (e.g.
                            Vista — no fixed price, no purchasable variant in the matcher's
                            sense). Such a package's "Kies X" is always a plain link to
                            `lead_url` (ignoring `embedded`), and — this is the important
                            part, see recommend() — it can only ever WIN the recommendation
                            when more of its cards are selected than of any other package; a
                            tie involving it excludes it and falls back to the ordinary
                            highest-selected-tier rule among the rest.
                            Default '' (no such package — Langer Thuis has none).
    lead_url                href for a lead_only_pkgs package's "Kies X" AND for the advice
                            bar's own CTA when that package is the live recommendation (see
                            the JS's leadPkgs handling). Mijn Thuis passes '#mijn-thuis-vista'
                            — a same-page hash the Oplossingen page's own tab deep-link
                            handler (`applyHash()`/`focusVista()`) already resolves into
                            "select the Mijn Thuis panel, scroll to and focus Vista's real
                            lead form" — no second lead form is built here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign check = '<span class="yes"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>'
  assign no = '<span class="no" aria-hidden="true">–</span>'
  assign arrow = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>'
  assign opl = opl_url | default: '/pages/oplossingen'
  assign tag_inzicht = tagline_inzicht | default: 'Rust, weet dat het goed gaat'
  assign tag_zeker = tagline_zeker | default: 'Vroeg weten geeft rust'
  assign tag_beschermd = tagline_beschermd | default: 'Snelle hulp bij een val of noodsituatie'
  assign match_badge = match_badge | default: 'Past bij uw situatie'
  assign recommended = recommended_pkg | default: 'zeker'
  assign pm_coll = collections[collection]
  if pm_coll == blank or pm_coll.products_count == 0
    assign pm_coll = collections['langer-thuis']
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Default pkg_meta: today's 3 Langer Thuis packages. Their display names come from
  pricing.config.json via `package_names` (see snippets/zv-package-name.liquid), never the
  product title; the literal names are only a fallback for a caller that doesn't pass it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture name_inzicht -%}{%- render 'zv-package-name', finder_key: 'aware', names: package_names -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture name_zeker -%}{%- render 'zv-package-name', finder_key: 'aware_plus', names: package_names -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture name_beschermd -%}{%- render 'zv-package-name', finder_key: 'care', names: package_names -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign name_inzicht = name_inzicht | strip | default: 'Inzicht' -%}
{%- assign name_zeker = name_zeker | strip | default: 'Zeker' -%}
{%- assign name_beschermd = name_beschermd | strip | default: 'Beschermd' -%}
{%- assign pkg_meta_str = pkg_meta -%}
{%- if pkg_meta_str == blank -%}
  {%- capture pkg_meta_str -%}
    inzicht|{{ name_inzicht }}|{{ zv_inzicht_monthly | remove: ' ' }}|/mnd|{{ tag_inzicht }}§zeker|{{ name_zeker }}|{{ zv_zeker_monthly | remove: ' ' }}|/mnd|{{ tag_zeker }}§beschermd|{{ name_beschermd }}|{{ zv_beschermd_monthly | remove: ' ' }}|/mnd|{{ tag_beschermd }}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign pkg_meta_arr = pkg_meta_str | strip | split: '§' -%}
{%- assign lead_list = lead_only_pkgs | default: '' | split: ',' -%}

{%- comment -%} per-instance TIER/NAMES for the JS, so 2 differently-vocabularied matchers can coexist on one page (see assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.js) {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture pm_tier_attr -%}
  {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}{%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}{%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{{ f[0] }}:{{ forloop.index }}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture pm_names_attr -%}
  {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}{%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}{%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{{ f[0] }}:{{ f[1] }}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%} package id -> real product, via custom.finder_key (same mapping as zv-checkout-overview) {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign fk_pairs = finder_key_map | default: 'aware:inzicht,aware_plus:zeker,care:beschermd' | split: ',' -%}
{%- capture pm_products -%}
  {%- assign first = true -%}
  {
  {%- for p in pm_coll.products -%}
    {%- assign fk = p.metafields.custom.finder_key.value -%}
    {%- assign pid = '' -%}
    {%- for pair in fk_pairs -%}
      {%- assign kv = pair | split: ':' -%}
      {%- if kv[0] == fk -%}{%- assign pid = kv[1] -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if pid != blank -%}
      {%- assign v = p.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
      {%- capture short_name -%}{%- render 'zv-package-name', finder_key: fk, names: package_names -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign short_name = short_name | strip -%}
      {%- if short_name == blank -%}{%- assign short_name = p.title | remove_first: pm_coll.title | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        variantId is what add-to-cart adds: the real package product, at the promo quantity
        (the 3 prepaid months, see assets/zv-vergelijk-pakketten.js). handle maps it to its
        installGroup in the pricing config, which decides whether the Climax installation
        line is added too (see CLAUDE.md Pricing pipeline).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}{%- assign first = false -%}
      {{ pid | json }}:{"variantId":{{ v.id | json }},"handle":{{ p.handle | json }},"sku":{{ v.sku | json }},"name":{{ short_name | json }},"line":{{ pm_coll.title | json }},"available":{{ p.available | default: false }},"url":{{ p.url | json }}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  }
{%- endcapture -%}

<div class="zv-vergelijk zv-pakket-matcher">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- if scenarios.size > 0 -%}
      <!-- PAKKET-MATCHER -->
      <div class="pm" data-pm-root data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}" data-activation-variant-id="{{ activation_variant_id }}" data-pm-tier="{{ pm_tier_attr | strip | escape }}" data-pm-names="{{ pm_names_attr | strip | escape }}" data-pm-lead-pkgs="{{ lead_only_pkgs | escape }}" data-pm-lead-url="{{ lead_url | escape }}">
        <script type="application/json" data-pm-products>{{ pm_products | strip }}</script>
        <div class="pm-head">
          <h3>{{ pm_heading | default: 'Welk pakket past bij uw situatie?' | escape }}</h3>
          {%- if pm_sub != blank -%}<p>{{ pm_sub | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="pm-cards" role="group" aria-label="{{ pm_heading | default: 'Welk pakket past bij uw situatie?' | escape }}">
          {%- for r in (1..3) -%}
            {%- assign row_str = r | append: '' -%}
            {%- capture row_html -%}
              {%- for b in scenarios -%}
                {%- assign b_row = b.settings.row | default: '1' -%}
                {%- if b_row == row_str -%}
                  <button type="button" class="pm-card" aria-pressed="false" data-pm-card data-pm-pkg="{{ b.settings.package }}" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="pm-card__t">{{ b.settings.title | escape }}</span>
                    {%- if b.settings.quote != blank -%}<span class="pm-card__q">{{ b.settings.quote | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  </button>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if row_html contains 'pm-card' -%}<div class="pm-row">{{ row_html }}</div>{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <div class="pm-advies" data-pm-advies hidden>
          <span class="pm-advies__chk" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4.5 12.5l5 5 10-11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <p class="pm-advies__txt"><b>{{ advies_label | default: 'Ons advies:' | escape }} <span data-pm-name></span>.</b> <span data-pm-tagline></span></p>
          <div class="pm-advies__cta">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--gold" data-pm-add data-label="{{ cta_label | default: 'Voeg [pakket] toe aan winkelwagen' | escape }}" data-added="{{ cta_added | default: 'Toegevoegd ✓' | escape }}"><span data-pm-add-text></span>{{ arrow }}</button>
            <a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" data-pm-viewcart hidden>{{ cta_view_cart | default: 'Bekijk winkelwagen' | escape }}{{ arrow }}</a>
            <a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ lead_url | escape }}" data-pm-lead-cta hidden><span data-pm-lead-text></span>{{ arrow }}</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pm-advies__err" data-pm-err role="alert" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-pm-status></p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="cmp-tbl" data-pm-table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="min-width:220px"><span class="visually-hidden">Kenmerk</span></th>
            {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}
              {%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}
              {%- assign pid = f[0] -%}
              {%- assign is_rec = false -%}
              {%- if pid == recommended -%}{%- assign is_rec = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              <th class="plan{% if is_rec %} rec{% endif %}" scope="col" data-pm-pkg="{{ pid }}">
                <span class="pm-badge">{{ match_badge | escape }}</span>
                {%- if is_rec -%}<span class="badge">Meest gekozen</span>{%- endif -%}
                <span class="pn">{{ f[1] }}</span>
                <span class="price">{{ f[2] }}{% if f[3] != blank %}<span>{{ f[3] }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
              </th>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="feat">Meest geschikt voor<small>Waar dit pakket het sterkst in is</small></td>
            {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}
              {%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}
              <td class="val txt tag" data-pm-pkg="{{ f[0] }}" data-pm-tagline-for="{{ f[0] }}">{{ f[4] | escape }}</td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
          {%- comment -%} feat | small | val1 | val2 | … (one val per pkg_meta_arr entry, same order) — § splits rows, | splits fields {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign rows = feature_rows | default: 'Discrete sensoren|Beweging en routine, geen camera|y|y|y§App voor familie|Meldingen delen met mantelzorgers|y|y|y§Melding bij afwijking|Alleen als er iets verandert|Dag|y|y§Dag- en nachtinzicht|24-uurs patroonherkenning|n|y|y§Meerdere contactpersonen|Familie samen op de hoogte|n|y|y§Meldkameropvolging|Nederlandse meldkamer, 24/7|n|n|y§Alarmknop met opvolging|Directe hulp bij nood|n|n|y§Jaarlijks onderhoud|Systeem blijft betrouwbaar|y|y|y' | strip | split: '§' -%}
          {%- for row in rows -%}
            {%- assign r = row | split: '|' -%}
            <tr>
              <td class="feat">{{ r[0] }}<small>{{ r[1] }}</small></td>
              {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}
                {%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}
                {%- assign ci = forloop.index0 | plus: 2 -%}
                {%- assign v = r[ci] -%}
                {%- if v == 'y' -%}<td class="val txt" data-pm-pkg="{{ f[0] }}">{{ check }}</td>
                {%- elsif v == 'n' -%}<td class="val txt" data-pm-pkg="{{ f[0] }}">{{ no }}</td>
                {%- else -%}<td class="val txt" data-pm-pkg="{{ f[0] }}">{{ v }}</td>{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </tr>
          {%- endfor -%}
          <tr class="cta">
            <td></td>
            {%- for pm in pkg_meta_arr -%}
              {%- assign f = pm | split: '|' -%}
              {%- assign pid = f[0] -%}
              {%- assign pname = f[1] -%}
              {%- assign is_rec = false -%}
              {%- if pid == recommended -%}{%- assign is_rec = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign is_lead = false -%}
              {%- if lead_list contains pid -%}{%- assign is_lead = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              <td{% if is_rec %} class="rec-cell"{% endif %} data-pm-pkg="{{ pid }}">
                {%- if is_lead -%}
                  <a class="btn {% if is_rec %}btn--gold{% else %}btn--ghost{% endif %}" href="{{ lead_url | escape }}" data-pm-lead="{{ pid }}">Kies {{ pname }}{% if is_rec %} {{ arrow }}{% endif %}</a>
                {%- elsif embedded -%}
                  <button type="button" class="btn {% if is_rec %}btn--gold{% else %}btn--ghost{% endif %}" data-pm-choose="{{ pid }}">Kies {{ pname }}{% if is_rec %} {{ arrow }}{% endif %}</button>
                {%- else -%}
                  <a class="btn {% if is_rec %}btn--gold{% else %}btn--ghost{% endif %}" href="{{ opl }}">Kies {{ pname }}{% if is_rec %} {{ arrow }}{% endif %}</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {%- if embedded -%}<div class="pm-tbl-err" data-pm-tbl-err role="alert" hidden></div>{%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
